Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Can We Calculate a Transformer by Hand?", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"5ba09387-2d50-41f8-8187-663119f52345"],

Cell["\<\
A tiny transformer language model, worked entirely by hand \[LongDash] from \
\"run casing\" to a probability for \"shoe\"\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"7d25a35d-4e63-4618-ae79-f9063e321e67"],

Cell["\<\
Modern language models contain billions of parameters and perform trillions \
of arithmetic operations per response. Nobody reproduces that by hand, and \
nobody needs to \[LongDash] but the arithmetic itself is not exotic. It is \
addition, multiplication, exponentials, and logarithms, arranged in a \
particular pattern called a transformer.

This notebook shrinks that pattern down until every number fits on a sheet of \
paper. I use a vocabulary of 6 words, sequences of 2 tokens, and an embedding \
dimension of 2. The whole model has a few dozen parameters. Every matrix \
multiplication, every softmax, every gradient below can be checked with a \
calculator.

The example is a drilling/completions phrase: given the two-word input \"run \
casing\", the model should predict that the next word is \"shoe\" (as in a \
casing shoe). This is a toy transformer LANGUAGE model \[LongDash] not an \
LLM, and not any kind of reproduction of ChatGPT or similar production \
systems. Its only job is to make the mechanics of attention, softmax, loss, \
and gradient descent completely visible.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9967490997185907`*^9, 
  3.996749100672472*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3f94e1a8-9945-4f71-8e3d-\
2897d2e0e3ee"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The shape of the calculation", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a48dedec-1be4-4845-808d-3f0a6e649aa9"],

Cell["\<\
Here is the full pipeline we are about to compute, start to finish. Every \
arrow below corresponds to a section of this notebook and an explicit matrix \
or vector calculation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d4ebbc7-e964-4df2-b18d-9bf4b1c026a9"],

Cell["\<\
\"run casing\"
    \[DownArrow]
Token IDs                    (Section 2)
    \[DownArrow]
Embeddings                   (Section 3)
    \[DownArrow]
Q, K, V                      (Section 4)
    \[DownArrow]
Scaled dot-product attention  (Sections 5-8)
    \[DownArrow]
Output representation        (Section 8)
    \[DownArrow]
Logits                       (Section 9)
    \[DownArrow]
Softmax probabilities        (Section 10)
    \[DownArrow]
Prediction: \"shoe\"?
    \[DownArrow]
Cross-entropy loss           (Section 11)
    \[DownArrow]
Gradient                     (Section 12)
    \[DownArrow]
Weight update                (Section 13)
    \[DownArrow]
New prediction                (Section 14)\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"84466a5b-e6d4-44ac-914f-f9934448403c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["What this notebook is \[LongDash] and is not", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"76892847-457d-4b58-8b7f-88d6878e3dcf"],

Cell["\<\
This is a transformer: the same attention-then-project pattern used by real \
language models, reduced to a size a person can compute by hand. It is a \
language model in the narrow technical sense of Section 1 below: something \
that assigns probabilities to \"what word comes next\". It is not an LLM (a \
large language model with billions of parameters trained on enormous text \
corpora), and it is not ChatGPT, Claude, or any production system. Treat \
every number in this notebook as belonging to a teaching-sized toy, not a \
scaled-down copy of a real product.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e9633408-78df-42c7-8eef-d4a65239eeaa"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["What we left out, and why that is fine here", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"df14f2cc-ee40-4dbd-8b5c-e5775457ba0d"],

Cell["\<\
LayerNorm \[LongDash] real transformers rescale activations between steps to \
keep training stable across many layers. With one block and tens of \
parameters, there is nothing to destabilize.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f462ccbc-091c-4f9c-b021-3a9105f2cf47"],

Cell["\<\
Residual (skip) connections \[LongDash] these help gradients flow through \
many stacked layers. We only have one layer, so there is no long path for a \
gradient to vanish along.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d1fb7c54-7f7f-410e-b343-852ed0d55a2d"],

Cell["\<\
Dropout \[LongDash] a regularizer that fights overfitting on large datasets. \
We have exactly one training example, so overfitting is not the concern; \
transparency is.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d3565a6b-ba64-4e34-aa7d-32d8820f7378"],

Cell["\<\
Multi-head attention \[LongDash] real models run several attention \
computations in parallel and combine them. One head already shows the \
complete mechanism; a second head would only duplicate arithmetic without \
adding a new idea.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"70abd356-d57c-4d1c-b040-b6d405f1a9fa"],

Cell["\<\
A large feed-forward network inside the block \[LongDash] omitted so that the \
output projection (Section 9) is the only place logits are produced, keeping \
the path from attention output to prediction short and traceable.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"006bf8c6-3ed2-484c-92a0-3402b6a9bd91"],

Cell["\<\
Positional encodings \[LongDash] with only 2 positions and a causal mask that \
already distinguishes \"first token\" from \"second token\", an explicit \
position signal would add notation without adding insight.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"979a9b30-03d8-466b-82f1-2e668f93c1c1"],

Cell["\<\
Every one of these choices trades realism for transparency. Section 16 \
returns to this trade-off explicitly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9735ffa-5717-4f65-91f3-4783b3c88c53"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. The Prediction Problem", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2dc9385c-4c6a-4b1d-9005-8367b293adea"],

Cell["\<\
Given the two-word phrase:

\"run casing\"

we want the model to predict the single most likely next word. In this \
drilling/completions example, the correct next word is:

\"shoe\"

(as in a casing shoe, the equipment run on the bottom of a casing string).

In plain language, a language model's job is to compute:

P(next token | previous tokens)

\[LongDash] read as \"the probability of the next token, given the tokens \
that came before it.\" The model does not know English, drilling engineering, \
or anything else. It only manipulates numbers derived from the input tokens, \
and those numbers happen to be arranged so that, after training, the right \
answer gets a high probability and everything else gets a low one. The rest \
of this notebook computes that probability distribution for \"run casing\" \
explicitly, one arithmetic step at a time, then shows how a single training \
update changes it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3fed41a5-8b94-489f-8ac1-443410cb0545"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Vocabulary and Token IDs", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"19c42f4a-484b-4f0a-a3ad-e41d3bdceb45"],

Cell["\<\
Computers do not work with words directly. The first step of any language \
model is to fix a vocabulary \[LongDash] a finite list of tokens the model \
knows about \[LongDash] and give every token an ID number (its position in \
the list). Any text the model sees must be built out of these tokens; \
anything outside the vocabulary simply cannot be represented.

Our vocabulary has 6 tokens: a beginning-of-sequence marker, three \
drilling-related words, one more drilling-related word, and an \
end-of-sequence marker.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4875c9c9-28c4-4089-bef5-86ffcbc2026c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Vocabulary", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<<BOS>\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<run\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<casing\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<shoe\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<cement\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<<EOS>\>\""}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Vocabulary", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "Vocabulary", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Token\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Token ID\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}],
    ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Background", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"LightGray", ",", " ", "None"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5d24ce0e-596c-4ced-8a88-460b1afacac5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"Token\"\>", "\<\"Token ID\"\>"},
    {"\<\"<BOS>\"\>", "1"},
    {"\<\"run\"\>", "2"},
    {"\<\"casing\"\>", "3"},
    {"\<\"shoe\"\>", "4"},
    {"\<\"cement\"\>", "5"},
    {"\<\"<EOS>\"\>", "6"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.85], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747453920336*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[2]=",ExpressionUUID->"b6418874-1bc0-4665-8577-d12e628d92a1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Our input phrase \"run casing\" is a sequence of two tokens. Looking up each \
word's position in the list above turns the phrase into a list of token IDs:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a6ee300-1a53-422b-bd1a-95a142f5c8a5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"inputTokens", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<run\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<casing\>\""}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"tokenIDs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Vocabulary", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
    " ", "inputTokens"}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"604a8f21-fae5-4fe2-b9e3-7f39460d6f29"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9967474540654793`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[4]=",ExpressionUUID->"a3687fb1-61ee-4ef2-b584-18c15149daa1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
So \"run casing\" becomes {2, 3}: \"run\" is token 2 and \"casing\" is token \
3. From this point on, the model never sees the words \"run\" or \"casing\" \
again \[LongDash] only the numbers 2 and 3, and (next) the vectors those \
numbers point to.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"680df650-90a5-4127-b29f-c3685c8324c7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Embedding Lookup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7811da34-882e-4b96-83da-af7af6cd504a"],

Cell["\<\
A token ID like 2 is just a label \[LongDash] it carries no information about \
meaning or similarity between words. An embedding replaces each token ID with \
a vector of numbers (here, a vector of length 2) that the model can actually \
do arithmetic with. In a real model these vectors are learned from data and \
have hundreds of dimensions; here we fix them by hand, with dimension 2, so \
every coordinate can be inspected directly.

Below is the full embedding table: one row per vocabulary token, one column \
per embedding dimension.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe843dd9-d81f-4eaf-8dd7-ddb627c7f820"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"EmbeddingMatrix", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<", "BOS", ">"}], "  ", "*)"}], "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", "run", "    ", "*)"}], "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", "casing", " ", "*)"}], "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", "shoe", "   ", "*)"}], "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", "cement", " ", "*)"}], "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "   ", 
    RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
     RowBox[{"<", "EOS", ">"}], "  ", "*)"}], "\n", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Vocabulary", ",", " ", "EmbeddingMatrix"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Token\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Embedding\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Background", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"LightGray", ",", " ", "None"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e16eca72-27ae-435e-8ceb-006243464382"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"Token\"\>", "\<\"Embedding\"\>"},
    {"\<\"<BOS>\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]},
    {"\<\"run\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]},
    {"\<\"casing\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]},
    {"\<\"shoe\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]},
    {"\<\"cement\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "1"}], "}"}]},
    {"\<\"<EOS>\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.85], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9967474540674057`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[6]=",ExpressionUUID->"25666447-9c5d-4f77-a29e-0a79390f8f61"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
\"run\" is deliberately set to {1, 0} and \"casing\" to {0, 1} \[LongDash] \
the two simplest possible distinct vectors in 2 dimensions. Selecting the \
rows for our input tokens {2, 3} builds the input matrix X: row 1 is the \
embedding of position 1 (\"run\"), row 2 is the embedding of position 2 \
(\"casing\"), and the 2 columns are the 2 embedding dimensions.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"416a4a53-f983-498d-8f1b-6a2f6c12446b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"X", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"EmbeddingMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "tokenIDs", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "X", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"682d106e-c061-494d-b297-5c174c249e8a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"1", "0"},
     {"0", "1"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454072998*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[8]//MatrixForm=",ExpressionUUID->"c75d8cc3-2ee6-4343-b610-\
9ca52a1150a4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "X", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"02c827e3-d1b8-4368-838c-dc09f29e0d79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9967474540752487`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[9]=",ExpressionUUID->"cb1da70d-bf7e-4d5f-ba2b-7359962018f4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
X is 2\[Times]2: 2 rows because our sequence has 2 tokens, 2 columns because \
our embedding dimension is 2. Because \"run\" and \"casing\" happen to be the \
two standard unit vectors, X is exactly the 2\[Times]2 identity matrix \
\[LongDash] a convenient coincidence that will make the next multiplications \
easy to check by hand, without changing what the multiplication means.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26dba138-9441-4beb-a0db-e15c16d9b66c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Query, Key, and Value Matrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"db9b335f-3274-460c-9568-8116f780352a"],

Cell["\<\
Attention compares positions to each other using three vectors derived from \
each position's embedding, called the query, key, and value. These are just \
names for the results of three ordinary matrix multiplications \[LongDash] \
there is no decision-making or comparison happening yet, only arithmetic that \
sets up the comparison in Section 5.

We fix three 2\[Times]2 weight matrices, WQ, WK, WV, by hand:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8fb578f0-9859-4547-a026-48b278bc9d2f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"WQ", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"WK", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"WV", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "WQ", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<      \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "WK", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<      \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "WV", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4a043668-a4f0-422f-b0cf-5eb03af013c0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"1", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"      \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "1"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"      \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454080777*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[13]=",ExpressionUUID->"61cc26c5-4e82-4278-9f14-578e45ac6a44"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Query Q = X . WQ. Each row of Q is a row of X (a token's embedding) \
multiplied against the columns of WQ, entry-by-entry sum of products \
\[LongDash] ordinary matrix multiplication:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"49f41177-ec7f-4a9b-8037-1f3373b4504d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Q", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"X", ".", "WQ"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "X", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   .   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "WQ", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   =   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "Q", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dfa6d2d6-45f5-481e-b61d-628803978fd0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   .   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"1", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   =   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"1", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454082818*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[15]=",ExpressionUUID->"f54392bd-40e3-487f-9674-c4f8fa1be5c4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Key K = X . WK, computed the same way:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ccda2dab-3b72-47ab-a1e1-bfe05ca75a1c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"K", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"X", ".", "WK"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "X", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   .   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "WK", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   =   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "K", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a30a1caf-c1c7-45ec-9851-cc95209d38d3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   .   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "1"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   =   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "1"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9967474540883427`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[17]=",ExpressionUUID->"f9f6a9b9-5678-44e8-b59e-56a667b68669"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Value V = X . WV, computed the same way:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"37c55928-6e61-41b7-a320-586a166b7f89"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"V", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"X", ".", "WV"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "X", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   .   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "WV", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   =   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "V", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d0d726b3-aaaa-402b-b7f2-760e8d0bfff5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   .   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   =   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454090437*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[19]=",ExpressionUUID->"db91a610-c225-4820-aabe-eacc3a6a8152"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Because X is the identity matrix (Section 3), each product above equals the \
corresponding weight matrix exactly (Q = WQ, K = WK, V = WV). You can verify \
this by hand: row 1 of X, {1,0}, times WQ picks out row 1 of WQ; row 2, \
{0,1}, picks out row 2. With a less convenient X the arithmetic is the same, \
just less obviously so.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9cb1b1a-431d-4191-879c-4166622b9026"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Attention Scores", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e79bb574-535e-4e94-936c-813ded478d72"],

Cell["\<\
To measure how much position 2 should attend to position 1 (and to itself), \
we compare Q to K using a matrix product: Q . Transpose[K]. Each entry (i, j) \
of the result is the dot product of query i with key j \[LongDash] a single \
number summarizing how well they align.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b43cd784-a6ad-4de3-a6a3-dd7bae2433d4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rawScores", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Q", ".", 
    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "K", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "Q", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   .   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "K", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   =   \>\"",
     ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "rawScores", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0f5aa31a-77c4-49eb-af29-2fbede1fd9bb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"1", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   .   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"1", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   =   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"2", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454095748*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[21]=",ExpressionUUID->"3d24ab89-e992-40f3-8535-05dfbf2ea2a0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Before using these numbers, we scale them down by Sqrt[d], where d = 2 is the \
embedding dimension. Why: as d grows, dot products of random vectors tend to \
grow larger in magnitude purely because more terms are being added up, which \
would push the softmax in Section 7 toward extremely peaked (near one-hot) \
outputs and make training unstable. Dividing by Sqrt[d] keeps the scores in a \
stable, comparable range regardless of dimension.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6cdb57f6-d613-4a6e-afab-387b53cc2519"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", "2"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"scaledScores", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rawScores", "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "d", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "scaledScores", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:=",ExpressionUUID->"162adeb4-9690-4c59-a2e4-34db3194bf80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"0.7071067811865475`", "0.`"},
     {"1.4142135623730951`", "0.7071067811865475`"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454097995*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[24]//MatrixForm=",ExpressionUUID->"a597b663-43bf-451e-9635-\
0627cef3bc39"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Causal Mask", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9400ddb1-ab68-4cf6-aa08-b0f3dbce077b"],

Cell["\<\
This is a next-token predictor: for every position, we ask it to predict the \
token that comes after that position. If position 1 (\"run\") were allowed to \
look at position 2 (\"casing\") while trying to predict what comes after \
\"run\", it would effectively be allowed to see part of the very continuation \
it is supposed to predict \[LongDash] not a fair test, and not how the model \
will be used at inference time, one token at a time.

A causal mask enforces this: position i may attend only to positions j \
\[LessEqual] i. We implement the mask by replacing every disallowed (future) \
entry with -\[Infinity], so that after the softmax in Section 7 those \
positions receive exactly zero attention weight.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b3a3dfe-d5ef-4b3d-8ffb-a69ea49e6bd5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"maskedScores", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"scaledScores", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}]}], "}"}], ",", "        ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"position", " ", "1", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", "\"\<run\>\"", ")"}]}], ":", " ", 
       RowBox[{"position", " ", "2", " ", "is", " ", "masked"}]}], " ", 
      "*)"}], "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"scaledScores", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"scaledScores", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "  ", 
    RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"position", " ", "2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", "\"\<casing\>\"", ")"}]}], ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"both", " ", "positions", " ", "allowed"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n",
     "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "maskedScores", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4a18c0f3-3e99-429e-a8da-d6188193ff8a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"0.7071067811865475`", 
      RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}]},
     {"1.4142135623730951`", "0.7071067811865475`"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9967474541032553`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[26]//MatrixForm=",ExpressionUUID->"c378d3eb-4b49-40a0-af6c-\
0ff5297ab054"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Compare this to the unmasked scaledScores above: only the top-right entry \
changed, from a finite number to -\[Infinity]. That single entry is exactly \
the score for \"position 1 attending to position 2\" \[LongDash] the one \
comparison a causal, left-to-right model is never allowed to make. Position 2 \
keeps both of its entries, because when predicting the token after \
\"casing\", the model is entitled to use everything up to and including \
\"casing\".\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b5ff5bf-4dd7-4ff9-b6ad-46ad86b38c06"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7. Softmax", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9cbbce4d-6fa6-4d50-92f2-23e46d63fca1"],

Cell["\<\
Attention scores need to become a probability distribution \[LongDash] \
non-negative numbers that sum to 1 \[LongDash] so they can be used as weights \
in Section 8. Softmax does this:

Softmax[z_i] = Exp[z_i] / Sum[Exp[z_j], {j}]

Every score is exponentiated (so all results are positive), then divided by \
the sum of all the exponentials in that row (so the row sums to exactly 1). \
Let's do this by hand for row 2 (the \"casing\" row), the one with two real \
numbers to compare:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56291b84-3b05-4cef-abcf-0a60698a2762"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"row2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"maskedScores", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"exps", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Exp", "[", "row2", "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5b3ed1a5-3e5a-44f8-b1e8-a45ee6509f22"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"4.1132503787829275`", ",", "2.028114981647472`"}], "}"}]], "Output",\

 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454105163*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[28]=",ExpressionUUID->"ebcf7dd9-eb12-4bc4-a5a8-1d28c423eccf"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sumExps", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Total", "[", "exps", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9a30458d-e93e-4dca-ace3-4fcf699bf4d8"],

Cell[BoxData["6.1413653604304`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454110076*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[29]=",ExpressionUUID->"33670950-74fe-4fec-9743-fa0a7d2ef9ae"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"softmaxRow2", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"exps", "/", "sumExps"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:=",ExpressionUUID->"fb5be867-011d-476d-8a0c-57de8528e93e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"0.669761549326657`", ",", "0.33023845067334306`"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454111952*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[30]=",ExpressionUUID->"fd371eff-3016-4d04-965d-9b992304f3ba"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Total", "[", "softmaxRow2", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e5891e08-3e70-473f-929e-184e3c39c438"],

Cell[BoxData["1.`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9967474541135817`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[31]=",ExpressionUUID->"5c4f8f6d-c661-485d-89bd-2e97dbf55f3e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The two exponentials are ~4.113 and ~2.028; dividing each by their sum ~6.141 \
gives probabilities ~0.670 and ~0.330, which do sum to 1 (up to \
floating-point rounding). Now apply the same formula, row by row, to the \
whole masked score matrix (row 1 is trivial: exp[x]/exp[x] = 1 for the only \
allowed entry, and 0 for the masked one):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb4ec268-1ca3-47ff-9819-00188325a15e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SoftmaxRow", "[", "row_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"finite", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "ex"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"finite", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
        RowBox[{"row", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", " ", ">", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", "finite", "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ex", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"If", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", " ", ">", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{"#", " ", "-", " ", "m"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], 
         " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "row"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ex", "/", 
       RowBox[{"Total", "[", "ex", "]"}]}]}]}], "\n", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"attentionWeights", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SoftmaxRow", " ", "/@", " ", "maskedScores"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "attentionWeights", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3cc3d363-2dcc-4d21-9422-3ba22d10dd45"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"1.`", "0.`"},
     {"0.6697615493266569`", "0.330238450673343`"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454115452*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[34]//MatrixForm=",ExpressionUUID->"8178d41d-7b36-481e-bc33-\
72afb6209744"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Total", " ", "/@", " ", "attentionWeights"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:=",ExpressionUUID->"210bcc66-210d-477d-bd43-15a903857328"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1.`", ",", "0.9999999999999999`"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454120277*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[35]=",ExpressionUUID->"369f6dca-93e3-4479-bc1e-77f73934673d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Both rows sum to 1, confirming attentionWeights is a valid pair of \
probability distributions. Row 1 is {1, 0}: position 1 puts all of its \
attention on itself, because the causal mask left it no other choice. Row 2 \
is approximately {0.670, 0.330}: position 2 splits its attention mostly onto \
position 1 (\"run\"), with some weight on itself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76e01916-617f-477b-93a8-291144ab98ba"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8. Weighted Values", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"409220e5-0e00-4ec6-87b9-373af9079714"],

Cell["\<\
Attention weights tell us how much to blend the value vectors of each \
position. The blend itself is one more matrix multiplication:

AttentionOutput = AttentionWeights . V\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8990e19f-4f51-4e02-b597-7f5ffb9f1d52"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"attentionOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"attentionWeights", ".", "V"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "attentionWeights", "]"}], ",", 
    " ", "\"\<   .   \>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "V", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<   =   \>\"", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "attentionOutput", "]"}]}], "}"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1a263b4a-8764-4f8f-a48e-61a1512ea3bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1.`", "0.`"}, {"0.6697615493266569`", "0.330238450673343`"}},
        RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1, RowAlignments -> Baseline, 
       ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   .   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1,
        RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", 
      ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], "\"   =   \"", 
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", 
      GridBox[{{"1.`", "0.`"}, {"0.6697615493266569`", "0.330238450673343`"}},
        RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1, RowAlignments -> Baseline, 
       ColumnAlignments -> Center], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}], 
    Function[BoxForm`e$, 
     MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996747454121949*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[37]=",ExpressionUUID->"9c13c0a3-7982-4100-b873-81c37acea65e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Row 1 of the result equals V's row 1 exactly (\"run\"'s own value vector), \
since row 1 of attentionWeights was {1,0}. Row 2 is a genuine blend: about \
67% of V's row 1 plus 33% of V's row 2. This row \[LongDash] the \
representation built at position 2, after mixing in information from position \
1 under the causal mask \[LongDash] is what we use to predict the token that \
comes after \"casing\":\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f39236eb-c3a1-47fb-bb1b-b1116d9ec7e1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"h", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"attentionOutput", "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:=",ExpressionUUID->"732eb7c9-764a-4da1-a6c1-d45cd5bdda5e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"0.6697615493266569`", ",", "0.330238450673343`"}], "}"}]], "Output",\

 CellChangeTimes->{3.9967474541267653`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[38]=",ExpressionUUID->"6e120dd8-2004-4595-8d58-25020c96d90f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9. Output Projection and Logits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7f90bbcc-84e7-4c78-98c0-450f8fe596da"],

Cell["\<\
h is a length-2 vector, but we need a score for every one of the 6 vocabulary \
tokens. The output projection matrix WOut (2 rows \[Times] 6 columns, one \
column per vocabulary token) does that conversion:

Logits = h . WOut\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02073108-673e-4c77-9a81-5614cc5dbbd7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"WOut", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", "  ", "1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "  ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "  ", "0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "\n", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "WOut", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ae9df04e-f7e0-4342-bb00-038cbfc89aac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"0", "1", "0", "1", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "0"},
     {"0", "0", "1", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "0", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
