Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["15. What Just Happened?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2a211b55-f8f3-432c-87c4-77f0b60cb8eb"],

Cell["\<\
The forward pass turned \"run casing\" into a full probability distribution \
over the vocabulary (Sections 2-10).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"dfc947d4-4c86-46e6-86ff-8cf9b4da07c3"],

Cell["\<\
We told the model the correct next token was \"shoe\", and cross-entropy loss \
measured exactly how wrong its distribution was (Section 11).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8765adc6-67c7-4912-bf52-ca6ead932efe"],

Cell["\<\
The gradient measured how each parameter of WOut would affect that loss if \
nudged (Section 12), and we checked that gradient numerically rather than \
taking it on faith.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f2a28c9b-c170-41a2-8936-67058ebac2a9"],

Cell["\<\
Gradient descent moved every weight a small step opposite its gradient \
(Section 13).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"be5bb138-6b75-43e3-865d-9dde96733f3e"],

Cell["\<\
Running the identical input, \"run casing\", through the updated weights \
produced a different, better distribution: higher P(\"shoe\"), lower loss \
(Section 14).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8b29271e-2d70-4800-b7ac-49d0f37eb313"],

Cell["\<\
That loop \[LongDash] predict, measure error, compute gradient, update \
weights, predict again \[LongDash] is the numerical core of how transformer \
language models learn. Real training repeats it millions or billions of \
times, over enormous datasets, updating every parameter in the network (not \
just an output projection), with additional machinery (Section 16) layered on \
top. This notebook does not claim that a single hand-worked update on one \
example captures everything about training a real model \[LongDash] only that \
the arithmetic at the heart of it is exactly this.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13318658-a030-4cb7-9b42-db4f5419149a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["16. Scale Comparison", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4e846386-0f94-4626-96ae-ad4570fbc04d"],

